================================================================================
ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS
================================================================================

worldmonitor — https://github.com/koala73/worldmonitor
    Licensed AGPL-3.0-only. The Singularity Atlas was inspired by worldmonitor's
    situational-awareness dashboard: the idea of a composite index built from
    weighted sub-indices, a layered 3D globe, per-stream panels, cross-stream
    correlation, LLM-synthesised briefs, and feed-health tracking.

    No worldmonitor source code is present in this repository. worldmonitor is
    TypeScript, Rust (Tauri) and Node; this project is an independently written
    Python application (FastAPI, LangGraph, Neo4j) with a zero-build vanilla-JS
    frontend. The two share no source, and their only common component is the
    third-party globe.gl library, which each uses directly. What was taken is
    the design idea, not the expression of it.

globe.gl — https://github.com/vasturiano/globe.gl
    MIT. 3D globe rendering in the dashboard frontend.

This project also builds on, and gratefully acknowledges, the maintainers of:
FastAPI and Starlette, Uvicorn, LangGraph, the Neo4j Python driver, feedparser,
httpx, APScheduler, Pydantic, pytest, and Ollama.

Public data sources polled by the ingest pipeline, each under its own terms:
arXiv, GDELT, the Hacker News Algolia API, The Space Devs' Launch Library,
and the public RSS feeds of OpenAI, Google DeepMind, MIT Technology Review,
Ars Technica, The Verge, VentureBeat, Import AI and Interconnects.


